# Kandelo patch rationale (S33)
#
# CommonJS and vm.compileFunction need exact parameter strings, reusable
# compiled stencils and body/hashbang locations. Stock CompileFunction does
# not expose the full contract; keep an entry into the original compiler
# rather than build another parser. The bridge's script/source registry now
# owns native-function classification. Only real compiler offsets remain
# in engine options, and Node never calls SpiderMonkey APIs directly.
#
# Source-only cleanup; not rebuilt or behavior-qualified. Retention remains
# subject to README.md: Future work: platform omissions.

